      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Salon Client Survey Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a salon client survey?\", \"a\": \"A salon client survey is a short set of questions a salon sends clients about a visit, such as the consultation, the result, the wait, and the price. The owner reads the answers to decide what to change and which client to call back after a bad visit.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a salon client survey?\", \"a\": \"Write one prompt for Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> that names your services and the score that should reach the owner. Emergent builds the survey and the database it fills, and a follow-up prompt adds a question or a weekly email. Start on the free tier, which covers building and publishing.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should I ask in a salon client survey?\", \"a\": \"Ask about the parts of the visit the salon controls. Cover how easy booking was, whether the stylist asked what the client wanted before starting, whether the result matched that request, and whether the price matched the quote. Add one question on whether the client plans to book again, and close with an open question on what to fix first.\"}, {\"q\": \"How soon after an appointment should a salon client survey go out?\", \"a\": \"Send it that evening, a few hours after the client leaves the chair. A color studio can add one question a week later about how the shade looks after a few washes. The timing works like a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/restaurant'>restaurant survey</a>: ask soon after the visit, and send no more than one reminder.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a salon client survey have?\", \"a\": \"Keep the survey after a routine visit to 4 or 5 questions: the service, the result, the booking, a rebook question, and one open comment. Save longer surveys, such as a vote on new services, for a few times a year. Emergent builds it as one question per screen, and a client answers each with one tap on a phone.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a salon client survey ask for the client's name?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as an optional field. A name lets the owner call back a client who scored the color match low, while an anonymous comment cannot get a reply. With the field optional, clients who want a call leave their name, and the rest still answer without one.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a salon client survey ask whether clients would recommend the salon?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as one question near the end. The question behind every <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/nps'>nps survey</a> asks how likely the client is to recommend you to a friend or colleague, and the Net Promoter System scores it on a zero-to-ten scale. Ask it the same way every month so the scores compare, and keep the rebook question beside it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a salon client survey find out why clients stopped booking?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if it goes to overdue clients and asks them directly in 3 questions or fewer. Set overdue from each client's habit: a client booked every 5 weeks is overdue at 8, and a twice-a-year color client is not. Offer fixed reasons plus an other box to keep answers countable. With the booking system connected by API, the app sends the survey the day a client goes overdue.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a salon client survey ask happy clients to leave an online review?\", \"a\": \"Not only the happy ones. Google's policy for Maps reviews names selectively soliciting positive reviews from customers among the things merchants may not do. Put the review link on the thank-you screen every client sees, whatever score they gave, and keep low scores going to the owner for a call back.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can a salon client survey compare feedback for each stylist?\", \"a\": \"Make the first question ask which stylist did the service, and every result can split by stylist. Keep the same rating questions for every chair, as in any <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/customer-satisfaction'>customer satisfaction survey</a>, and wait for about 20 answers per stylist before reading much into a gap. On Emergent, those answers sit in a database the salon owns.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
